text:
### Instruction:
Create a css style to set a border on the bottom side of the element.

### Response:
div {
  border-bottom: 2px solid #000;
}

### Instruction:
Create a CSS rule to apply a two-pixel red border to a text box.

### Response:
input[type="text"] {
  border: 2px solid red;
}

### Instruction:
Create a CSS style to highlight code blocks on a web page.

### Response:
pre {
  background-color: #f7f7f7;
  padding: 10px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 5px;
}

code {
  color: #f80;
  background-color: #fcfcfc;
  padding: 3px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 3px;
}

### Instruction:
Write a style rule to apply a border on the first and last elements of the document.

### Response:
*:first-child, *:last-child {
   border: 1px solid black;
}

### Instruction:
Design a CSS style to make an element a circle and have a red border

### Response:
#circle {
    width: 50px;
    height: 50px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid red;
}

### Instruction:
Write a CSS code snippet to apply a border to all p elements.

### Response:
p {
  border: 1px solid #000;
}

### Instruction:
Make the following CSS code work properly on the web page.

### Input:
.special {
    background-color: #eee;
    border: 2px solid #999;
}

### Response:
.special {
    background-color: #eee;
    border: 2px solid #999;
    padding: 10px;
    display: block;
}

### Instruction:
Write a CSS style to give a border of 3 pixels to the HTML element.

### Response:
html {
    border: 3px solid black;
}

### Instruction:
Create a CSS program to apply a blue border to all <div> elements

### Response:
div {
    border: 2px solid blue;
}

### Instruction:
Create a CSS style sheet to apply the following styles to a div element.

### Response:
div {
    width: 50%;
    padding: 30px;
    font-size: 20px;
    background-color: #EEE;
    border: 1px solid black;
}

### Instruction:
Write a CSS script to add a border to the 'Title' element on a webpage.

### Response:
#Title {
    border: 1px solid black;
}
